# GEDCOM data files (prevent accidental commit of large/private files).
# Case-folded: PAF, Legacy and Family Tree Maker write .GED, and git is
# case-sensitive here, so a bare *.ged leaves a real family tree stageable.
# The second rule catches the backup and archive forms (.ged.bak, .ged.gz,
# .ged.1) that a bare extension glob misses.
*.[Gg][Ee][Dd]
*.[Gg][Ee][Dd].*
!tests/fixtures/*.[Gg][Ee][Dd]

